  <h2 id="what-it-means">What PCB with Computer Science actually means</h2>

  <p>
    PCB with Computer Science is not a new stream.
  </p>

  <p>
    It is Physics, Chemistry, and Biology as your three core subjects, with Computer Science added as a 5th or 6th subject — a combination a growing number of CBSE and other Indian schools with computer labs now offer.
  </p>

  <p>
    The Class 11-12 Computer Science curriculum in most boards covers Python programming, database concepts, and basic computer organisation.
  </p>

  <p>
    That is not a trivial add-on.
  </p>

  <p>
    It is the exact starting toolkit that bioinformatics, computational biology, and health-data roles ask for — you are not learning to code from a standing start after 12th like most PCB-only students would be.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">The usual bad advice</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>Computer Science alongside PCB is "just for backup" and does not really count for anything.</li>
      <li>Taking CS means you are secretly leaning toward engineering, so you should have taken PCM instead.</li>
      <li>The subject combination itself will decide your career, so just wait and see what marks come.</li>
      <li>Bioinformatics is basically the same as biotechnology, so any biology degree will get you there.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout__footer">
      None of this tells you what Computer Science alongside PCB actually changes in terms of real eligibility, real career paths, or real skill advantage — which is the part that matters.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="eligibility-myth">The eligibility myth to kill first</h2>

  <p>
    Here is the single most expensive misunderstanding students carry into this decision.
  </p>

  <p>
    Computer Science as an additional Class 12 subject is not the same as Mathematics.
  </p>

  <p>
    JEE Main, most B.Tech Computer Science Engineering seats, and most biomedical engineering programmes require Mathematics as a compulsory Class 12 subject alongside Physics — full stop. Computer Science does not substitute for it in these eligibility rules.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    {eligibilityMythCards.map((card) => (
      <div class:list={['compare-card', `compare-card--${card.tone}`]}>
        <div class="compare-card__label">{card.title}</div>
        <ul>
          {card.items.map((item) => (
            <li>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      If the JEE and Maths-based engineering door genuinely matters to you, the real fix is checking whether adding Mathematics as a separate subject is realistic for your situation.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is a different subject combination — often called PCMB — with different trade-offs. It is not what a Computer Science elective gives you.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Always verify current eligibility rules on the official <a href="https://jeemain.nta.nic.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">JEE Main portal</a> and your target university's admission page before planning years around any one route.
  </p>

  <p>
    Want the fuller picture of what a missing Mathematics subject changes across every exam and degree, not just this specific CS combination? <a href="/blog/career-options/pcb-career-options-without-maths/">Career options with PCB without Maths</a> maps the complete landscape — CAT, CLAT, UPSC, banking, and data-adjacent bridge routes included.
  </p>

