  <h2 id="ai-edge">Where this combination has a real AI-era edge</h2>

  <p>
    PCB-with-CS students often assume AI mainly matters for pure coders.
  </p>

  <p>
    That is already outdated in this specific niche.
  </p>

  <p>
    Genomics, drug discovery, and clinical data work are some of the fastest-growing places where AI tools are fusing domain knowledge with code, not replacing either one. Pharma employers are naming AI/ML skills for trials, automation, and genomics as non-negotiable, not optional.
  </p>

  <div class="skill-levels">
    <div class="skill-level">
      <div class="skill-level__header skill-level__header--l1">Level 1 — right now</div>
      <ul class="skill-list">
        <li><span class="skill-dot skill-dot--l1"></span>Get genuinely fluent in the Python and database basics your CS subject already introduced — do not let that syllabus go stale.</li>
        <li><span class="skill-dot skill-dot--l1"></span>Practice explaining biology concepts clearly in plain English, since domain communication matters as much as code in this space.</li>
        <li><span class="skill-dot skill-dot--l1"></span>Build the habit of verifying what AI tools generate instead of trusting outputs blindly.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="skill-level">
      <div class="skill-level__header skill-level__header--l2">Level 2 — during college or early upskilling</div>
      <ul class="skill-list">
        <li><span class="skill-dot skill-dot--l2"></span>Learn R and basic statistics alongside Python — both show up repeatedly in bioinformatics and health-data job postings.</li>
        <li><span class="skill-dot skill-dot--l2"></span>Work with real or public biological/health datasets, not only toy classroom examples.</li>
        <li><span class="skill-dot skill-dot--l2"></span>Build one visible project — a dataset summary, a small model, or a health-data dashboard — that you can explain end to end.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="skill-level">
      <div class="skill-level__header skill-level__header--l3">Level 3 — for long-term leverage</div>
      <ul class="skill-list">
        <li><span class="skill-dot skill-dot--l3"></span>Use AI tools to direct and speed up analysis while keeping judgement and verification firmly human.</li>
        <li><span class="skill-dot skill-dot--l3"></span>Build business and stakeholder communication skill so your domain-plus-code work is understandable to non-technical decision-makers too.</li>
        <li><span class="skill-dot skill-dot--l3"></span>Make your work visible — a portfolio, GitHub, or published project — so your domain-plus-code combination is not hidden in silence.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

